bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    catalog_service_named_capability_syscall_mismatch_2026-08-11, 0, "2026-11-28 p3sweep6: reproduced (catalogue mints exact NetListen(80); no syscall implementation consumed it - owned_net_listen_broker_allows was never defined anywhere despite the pinned spec; any IpcConnect(net) holder could bind/listen any port). Fix: implemented + exported in src/os/kernel/ipc/syscall_ipc.spl per the pinned spec signature - non-net endpoints and non NET_BIND(2)/NET_LISTEN(3) methods pass through; otherwise requires the requester's exact CapabilityKind.NetListen(port) for the wire port (payload bytes 8..10), fail-closed on truncated input / missing / wrong-port capability; empty pledged set denies. Verification: probe 4/4 (was 3/4); new spec catalog_net_listen_capability_alignment 7/7; syscall_number_consistency 38/38; root_service_catalog_build_contract 2/2. Residuals: the doc's dynamic confinement specs still cannot LOAD (pre-existing circular import vmm vs vmm_vma - OS-owner lane); wiring the gate into the owned-send delivery path is an OS-lane design decision. close_evidence reproducer=test/01_unit/os/kernel/ipc/catalog_net_listen_capability_alignment_spec.spl prevention=test/01_unit/os/kernel/ipc/syscall_number_consistency_spec.spl"

